# Line endings: LF in the blobs, LF in every checkout.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF working copies, and a
# multi-line mutation anchor written with \n stops matching the file it is meant to sabotage.
# Measured before this file existed: the falsification harness reported 3/4 on a fresh Windows
# clone while the authoring tree was green -- the mutant was silently never applied.
# Forcing LF also keeps tools/git-hooks/pre-push a clean shell script everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
